rndis_iad_descriptor.bFunctionProtocol = rndis_opts->protocol;
Reason:
These assignments read the class, subclass, and protocol fields from `rndis_opts` without holding the `rndis_opts->lock` mutex. Since these fields can be concurrently modified via configfs, a race condition occurs where the descriptor values may be set with inconsistent or partially updated data, leading to incorrect USB descriptor configuration.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
scoped_guard(mutex, &rndis_opts->lock) {
    rndis_iad_descriptor.bFunctionClass = rndis_opts->class;
    rndis_iad_descriptor.bFunctionSubClass = rndis_opts->subclass;
    rndis_iad_descriptor.bFunctionProtocol = rndis_opts->protocol;
}
Reason:
The `scoped_guard` acquires the mutex before reading the options and automatically releases it after the block. This ensures that the three fields are read atomically from `rndis_opts`, preventing any race with concurrent configfs writes that could cause inconsistent descriptor values. The fix also requires the inclusion of `<linux/cleanup.h>` for the `scoped_guard` macro.

